course: dictionary
lesson: 5407
title: Lab: a short word with two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Lab is short for laboratory, a room or building where scientists do experiments and tests. «Goggles are worn in the school lab because eyes are delicate and some chemicals damage them in seconds.» The clue is goggles and chemicals, so the lab is a place where science work happens.
explain: Lab can also mean a Labrador, a large friendly dog. Use context to choose. Ask what would fit in the sentence: a room for experiments fits, but a friendly dog does not.
explain: Lab is informal, so people use it in everyday talk. Lab coat and lab rules are common phrases that use the short form.
fact: Lab is short for laboratory.
fact: A laboratory is a room or building where scientists do experiments and tests.
fact: Lab rules are safety rules: wear goggles, tie hair back, and have no food or drink.
fact: Lab can also mean a Labrador, a large friendly dog.
fact: «Every kitchen is a chemistry lab: heat, acid and water change food into new substances.»
exercise: «Goggles are worn in the school lab because eyes are delicate.» What is a lab here? | A bus stop | A large friendly dog | A kind of food | *A room where pupils and scientists do experiments
exercise: Which of these is a lab safety rule? | Shout to your friends across the room | Run between the tables | *Wear goggles and tie your hair back | Bring a snack to eat at the bench
exercise: Jaya says, «Our lab got a new Lab today!» What does the second lab mean? | A science room | *A Labrador, a large friendly dog | A bedroom | A type of coat
test: «In 1928 Alexander Fleming came back from a holiday to a messy lab.» What is a lab? | A park | A bedroom | *A room where scientists do experiments | A shop
test: What is the short form of laboratory? | *Lab | Ratory | Labo | Labrador
exam: Which sentence uses lab to mean a place for experiments? | *Goggles are worn in the school lab | Lab is a nice name for a cat | I had a lab sandwich for lunch | My lab loves to fetch sticks
